briefs.avoids:
Signal Galley's charges:
- periwinkle as off-period for an 80s CRT (feedback);
- the thick, 30px-rounded pewter slab (every lens, open since round 7);
- Chat times in two gutters (skeptic, system, interaction);
- 15% cyan day tiles reading teal (all);
- Status and Settings as near-copies of Galley Rack (skeptic, style, system);
- Coming up's missing leader and the 'WAS DUE / YESTERDAY' wrap (type);
- ring ticks that read as radio buttons (interaction);
- the mixed DM Sans and Plex Mono pairing (type);
- a faint afterglow and the squeezed radar words (soul).

Reverse Video's charges, avoided by taking only its best parts:
- the pale #89a2b5 block rivalling Send;
- shouting .88rem mono-caps legends;
- frame links that read as labels;
- double frames (none here);
- the typed-in field that lost its halo (kept here);
- Status at 18.7% green (Signal Galley's sage leads and lamps keep the green).

briefs.hypothesis:
A FIX FOR A PROMISING PALETTE THAT FELL SHORT FOR ONE CLEAR REASON.

Magic Eye (r8-rand-1) had the round's most admired structure:
- first with the style lens (8);
- the type lens's third pick (7.5), as 'the boldest real typesetting';
- interaction's best sight line: the whole Home in about 1.3 screens, the month on one screen, one-line To do rows.

Every lens that marked it down did so for its wine, rose and oxblood (feedback 3.3, soul 4.2, skeptic 4.5), and then for finish: the lost greeting pool, bracket buttons, underlined titles, proportional figures, empty margins and 43/56 small targets.

Skeptic, type and lessons.md all asked for this exact graft: 'programme-guide rows ... fitted into Signal Galley's slate frame, with Attract Mode's VT323 used only for field and weekday labels, would likely beat every entrant here on typography.'

This puts style's favourite structure into the feedback lens's favourite colours, and it is a real rival to the leaders because it is the only praised structure that is neither trays nor windows. It is clearly different from every carried palette:
- from Signal Galley's two-column trays and hung stations;
- from Reverse Video's framed windows;
- from Plotting Room's bays;
- from Magic Eye itself (whole-page colour).

It is also distinct from this round's Magic Eye mutant (wine with a serif), the Reverse Video x Magic Eye crossover (windows in wine) and the planetarium random (one centred serif column).

